{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782209024,"nonce":"DACw1LNMSWt0R+/sBXL5yfeJKaU=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGZ27ew","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/312","origin":"github"},"title":"FCU reports '3D gyro: Fail' (SYS_STATUS sensor-health) persistently from boot — 2026-06-22 Massabesic","message":"## Symptom\n\nDuring the 2026-06-22 Lake Massabesic deployment ([#309](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/309)), the operator noticed an **FCU health warning on the annunciator**. Decoded from the bag, it is the autopilot's SYS_STATUS sensor-health bitmask reporting **3D gyro: Fail**.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBag `gabby/logs/bizzyboat/2026-06-22T13-22-29+00-00`, topic `/diagnostics`:\n\n- `mavros: System` diagnostic at **ERROR** (\"Sensor health\") for **27,554 of 27,557** heartbeats — i.e. essentially the entire mission, **from boot (09:22:32)** through dock return.\n- Decoded `mavros: System` KeyValues:\n  - `Sensor present: 0x1230DC2B`, `Sensor enabled: 0x0220DC2B`, `Sensor health: 0x0230DD2A`\n  - **`3D gyro: Fail`**\n  - All others **Ok**: 3D accelerometer, absolute pressure, GPS, 3D angular rate control, attitude stabilization, yaw/position control, motor outputs/control, AHRS subsystem, Battery.\n- `mavros/state.connected` = **True** for the whole run (one boot transition at 09:22:31→32). So this is **not** a USB/comms flap (contrast the FCU↔gabby USB issue from #299) — the autopilot is reporting its **own** 3D gyro unhealthy.\n\n## Impact\n\nNo visible effect on the survey: the boat's primary attitude/heading source is the **SBG INS**, which was healthy all day (status green, RTK_INT). But the ArduPilot/CUAV autopilot ran the entire mission with a failed-gyro health flag, which is not nominal and would matter for any FCU-internal stabilization/failsafe behavior.\n\n## Next steps / questions\n\n- Confirm whether it's a specific IMU instance failing a consistency/health check (multi-IMU Cube/CUAV) or a genuine gyro fault — check ArduPilot `INSx` params, pre-arm, and the autopilot logs (`.bin`) for the same window.\n- Relationship to **#4** (ArduRover 4.5.7 → 4.6.3 upgrade; EKF3 fixes) — does the newer firmware clear it?\n- Possibly related: **#156** (SBG vs CUAV ellipsoidal-Z disagreement).\n\nPart of the #309 deployment follow-up.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}